# VGV workflow handoffs (dual-host)

This rule **does not replace** Wingspan skills. When `/brainstorm`,
`/plan`, `/build`, `/code-review`, or `/plan-technical-review` runs,
**that skill's SKILL.md is authoritative** for workflow steps and
handoff option lists.

This rule defines **how to present** those options (structured
question priority) and **how selections execute** per host.

## Structured question priority (required)

Always follow `vgv-ask-question.mdc` before showing handoff options:

| Priority | Tool | When |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | **AskQuestion** | In Cursor tool schema |
| 2 | **AskUserQuestion** | In Claude Code tool schema |
| 3 | **ask_user_question** | MCP `vgv-ask-question` — **only** if neither host tool exists |
| 4 | Numbered chat list | Silent last resort |

**Never call MCP** when AskQuestion or AskUserQuestion is available.

Map skill option lists to the canonical payload in
`references/structured-questions-protocol.md`. Skills markdown **Options**
blocks are tool input, not chat output.

## Handoff option lists (deduped for Cursor)

Upstream Claude skills may list a “clear context” twin next to “start in
place.” On **Cursor**, those are the same action — present the deduped
lists below. On **Claude Code**, offer clear-context variants when the
skill requests them.

**After brainstorm** (from brainstorm skill):

1. Plan now (Recommended)
2. Review and refine approach
3. Done for now

**After plan** (from plan skill — Wingspan ≥ v0.0.4):

1. Build now (Recommended)
2. Open the plan file in my code editor
3. Review and refine

**After plan-technical-review** — follow that skill's post-review
options (same dedupe: one Build now, not Start building).

**After build (mid-plan, more phases remain)** — Cursor only; never
offer clear-context:

1. Continue in this chat (Recommended)
2. Stop here

**After build (shipped)** — Done only unless the skill lists more.

Never paste these as numbered chat when a tier 1–3 structured question
tool is available. On Cursor, never display `Clear context`,
`Start building`, `Continue with planning`, or
`Clear context and continue` — those are Claude-only or broken on
Cursor.

## Host differences after the user picks

| Host | After selection |
| --- | --- |
| **Cursor** | Execute immediately in **this chat** — no `/clear`, no new chat |
| **Claude Code** | Follow the skill: same-chat **or** clear-context handoff when listed |

### Cursor execution table

| User selection | Cursor action |
| --- | --- |
| Plan now | Run **plan** skill on the brainstorm doc path |
| Build now | Run **build** skill on the plan file path |
| Continue in this chat | Loop **build** to the next plan phase in this chat |
| Stop here | End build; user runs `/build` again to resume from Status markers |
| Open the plan file in my code editor | `open docs/plan/<filename>.md` |
| Review and refine / Review and refine approach | Run **refine-approach** on the artifact |
| Freeform: run plan-technical-review | Run **plan-technical-review** on the plan path |
| Review (after `/build`) | Run **code-review** on the changed scope |
| Done for now / Done | Summarize artifact path; stop |

### Claude Code clear-context handoffs

When the skill offers `Clear context and plan`, `Clear context and
build`, or similar, those remain valid on Claude Code. Do not strip
them on Claude Code. On Cursor, translate per `vgv-ask-question.mdc`
(e.g. `Clear context and plan` → `Plan now`).

## When host AskQuestion / AskUserQuestion is missing

Follow `vgv-ask-question.mdc` silently:

1. MCP **`ask_user_question`** if registered and no host tool
2. Short numbered chat list only if MCP is also absent

Do not narrate the fallback. See `references/structured-questions-protocol.md`.

## Parent model routing (Cursor handoff phases)

Use the **chat model picker** for the parent agent on Cursor:

| Phase / role | Recommended parent model | Why |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Brainstorm / plan / refine (handoffs) | **Composer 2.5** (not Auto) | Best chance of native AskQuestion; fall back to MCP if absent |
| Build / implementation | Composer 2.5 or Claude Sonnet 5 | Coding strength; user preference |
| Avoid for handoffs | **Grok 4.5** | No AskQuestion |

Subagent `model:` pins in agent files are separate — do not override
in Task calls unless the user asks.

| Upstream tier | Cursor `model:` | Agents |
| --- | --- | --- |
| haiku | `composer-2.5` | `pr-readiness-review-agent` |
| sonnet | `claude-sonnet-5` | codebase, simplicity, test-quality, plan-splitting, research agents |
| inherit | `inherit` | vgv-review, architecture, user-flow, flutter-reviewer |

## `/review` vs `/code-review` (Cursor)

| Command | What it is |
| --- | --- |
| `/review` | Cursor built-in — Bugbot or Security only |
| `/code-review` | VGV Wingspan quality review (Claude `/review`) |

## Slash skills

Users can invoke `/plan`, `/build`, `/brainstorm`, `/code-review`, etc.
This rule does not remove slash commands — it fixes handoff
**presentation** (structured questions) and **execution** after phase
completion.

## Skill locations (marketplace only)

Wingspan ships via the **VGV Cursor Team Marketplace** plugin. No
repo-local link script or `.cursor/skill-custom` wiring.

| What | Where |
| --- | --- |
| Skills | Plugin `cursor/skills/` (exposed as `/brainstorm`, `/plan`, …) |
| Agents | Plugin `cursor/agents/` |
| Rules | Plugin `rules/` (this file, `vgv-ask-question.mdc`, …) |
| MCP | Plugin `mcp/vgv-ask-question-mcp/` via `mcp.json` |

**Install:** Cursor Settings → Plugins → Team Marketplace → enable
**vgv-wingspan** (or your org aggregator). **Cmd+Q** and reopen after
updates.

Consumer monorepos (e.g. Sea Trials) may aggregate this plugin with
team-specific plugins; skills still resolve from the marketplace
install, not from checked-in `.cursor/skills/` copies.

## Artifact YAML header

When writing new brainstorm or plan docs:

```yaml
vgv_next:
  skill: plan
  artifact: docs/brainstorm/YYYY-MM-DD-topic-brainstorm-doc.md
```

(or `skill: build` + plan path after planning)

User can `@`-attach the file and say: “Run the next skill from
`vgv_next`.”

## Optional: thread too long (Cursor)

Only if the user **asks** for a fresh session: new chat (Cmd+L /
Ctrl+L), then `/` → skill → `@` artifact. Not the default handoff.

